  <accessrestrict id="aspace_86d4698b84b171a24689fd124662fd4d">
    <head>Conditions Governing Access</head>
<p>Materials are open without restrictions.</p>  </accessrestrict>
  <arrangement id="aspace_613fd68a1e2a3f12899184f982127b91">
    <head>Arrangement</head>
<p>This collection is arranged into two series based on how they're housed. Series I contains rolled posters and is housed in three oversized boxes. Series II contains flattened posters and is housed in the oversized mapcase. Arrangement is solely based on format, rather than content and provenance.</p>  </arrangement>
  <bioghist id="aspace_71d7f8e8c0a4abc1c462ad4c3b8ae1c0">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>These oversized posters were unprocessed and on the shelves in the Poly Archives until 2026 when they were taken to NYU conservation to be treated. Some were flattened, others were rolled and rehoused into oversized boxes.</p>  </bioghist>
  <custodhist id="aspace_b4d06494bb535c022204e1db97327413">
    <head>Custodial History</head>
<p>There is no known provenance for any of the materials in this collection. Due to this, we created the collection based purely on format.</p>  </custodhist>
  <prefercite id="aspace_b5186ac10b89554e08b23629e4b1aee0">
    <head>Preferred Citation</head>
<p>Identification of item, Date; Poly Archives Poster and Floor-plan Collections; RG 071; Box number; Folder number or item identifier; Poly Archives at Bern Dibner Library of Science and Technology, New York University.</p>  </prefercite>
  <scopecontent id="aspace_334b1d7cdeda4f2b194d5a932251aad2">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>This collection includes posters and floor plans from both  Polytechnic University and NYU Poly. The floorplans include athletics (Jacobs Hall and Rogers Hall, 6 MetroTech Center), Dibner Library (5 MetroTech Center), and dormitory plans (Othmer Hall, 101 Johnson St) completed in the late 90s and early 2000s. The posters range from MTA maps, commemorative memorabilia, and miscellaneous classroom materials. 
 
Many of the items are undated. Floorplans we can date to the construction of the buildings. Branding and visual aesthetics indicate that many of the posters are from the 1990s.</p>  </scopecontent>
